1
00:00:00,163 --> 00:00:01,183
The oldest

2
00:00:01,183 --> 00:00:03,543
version of this method is actually from a book

3
00:00:03,543 --> 00:00:05,847
called "How to Read a Book"

4
00:00:05,847 --> 00:00:09,170
by Mortimer Adler from 1940.

5
00:00:09,170 --> 00:00:11,152
He calls it "inspectional

6
00:00:11,272 --> 00:00:11,982
reading."

7
00:00:11,982 --> 00:00:13,860
So you read chapter one,

8
00:00:13,860 --> 00:00:16,540
you study the contents page,

9
00:00:16,540 --> 00:00:17,800
the chapter

10
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:19,863
titles, the sub-headings,

11
00:00:20,080 --> 00:00:22,973
you skim a little to see how the author

12
00:00:22,973 --> 00:00:25,463
has laid out their argument.
